Z||000011||fieroshop||07-12-2000||12:59 AM||||One thing that I found out by installing those hod and side scoopsMy engine used to run in the area of 1/3 on the temp gauge and now it runs below the quarter mark. They do work and work well. Sure is nice to see my engine temp drop.<BR>By the way FieroGTgirl, if you have not been to a show you must go and see if not participate.<BR>Hey Terry I forgot to tell you. I talked with my machine guy and it looks like I will be cpming out with an anti-bump-steer kit after all. We are talking about a kit that all a person will need to do is take out the rear a-frames from an 87 back and we;d or have welded a bracket onto the a-fram. I will supply the bracket and also stainless steel tie rods along with poly-bushings and a step by step video that I will make showing how to install. The hood scoops will also have a vedeo showin how to cut and where your hood, also how to insert the piece and fiberglass it in place and work the necessary fillers and prime the hood. I think that will help a lot. Let me know what you think.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 07-12-2000).]||||reg||1
